workspace/skills/briefing/SKILL.md:49:1. Get the **briefing day's** conditions and forecast. Use the user's default city/country from session context.\n/root/.openclaw/workspace/skills/briefing/SKILL.md:64:1. **Title line** — compact: date, day-of-week, time. E.g. `Брифинг 14.02 (пт, 8:12)`. If briefing day is tomorrow, say so.\n/root/.openclaw/workspace/skills/briefing/SKILL.md:66:3. **Calendar** — briefing day's events, chronologically. Format: `HH:MM — Title`. All-day events first. If empty: one line noting no events.\n/root/.openclaw/workspace/skills/briefing/SKILL.md:113:- When briefing day is tomorrow, calendar and weather headers should reflect that.\n/root/.openclaw/workspace/skills/briefing/SKILL.md:122:- No call to action or question at the end. The briefing ends after the last section. No \"What's next?\", \"What's first?\", or similar.\n/root/.openclaw/workspace/skills/briefing/README.md:1:# briefing\n/root/.openclaw/workspace/skills/briefing/README.md:3:A daily briefing skill for OpenClaw. Gathers calendar events, active todos, and weather into a single concise message — optimized for mobile chat.\n/root/.openclaw/workspace/skills/briefing/README.md:7:When invoked (typically via `/briefing`), the agent:\n/root/.openclaw/workspace/skills/briefing/README.md:10:2. Determines whether the briefing covers **today** or **tomorrow** (based on current time and remaining events).\n/root/.openclaw/workspace/skills/briefing/README.md:18:This skill orchestrates three companion skills. All are optional — the briefing adapts to whatever is available.\n/root/.openclaw/workspace/skills/briefing/README.md:21:- [**`todo-management`**](https://clawhub.ai/lstpsche/todo-management) — Active/pending todo items. Provides task list for the briefing.\n/root/.openclaw/workspace/skills/briefing/README.md:44:If the briefing produces poor results, try a more capable model before adjusting the skill.\n/root/.openclaw/workspace/skills/briefing/README.md:64:This skill is triggered by the user via `/briefing` command. It is also available for the agent to invoke when contextually appropriate (e.g. as part of a scheduled cron job).\n/root/.openclaw/workspace/skills/briefing/README.md:66:## Recommended: scheduled daily briefing\n/root/.openclaw/workspace/skills/briefing/README.md:68:This skill works best as a **scheduled cron job** that fires every morning at your wake time. Instead of manually typing `/briefing` each day, let OpenClaw send it for you.\n/root/.openclaw/workspace/skills/briefing/README.md:73:openclaw cron add \\\n/root/.openclaw/workspace/skills/briefing/README.md:74:  --name \"Morning briefing\" \\\n/root/.openclaw/workspace/skills/briefing/README.md:75:  --cron \"0 7 * * *\" \\\n/root/.openclaw/workspace/skills/briefing/README.md:78:  --message 'Use the \"briefing\" skill for this request.' \\\n/root/.openclaw/workspace/skills/briefing/README.md:84:- `--cron \"0 7 * * *\"` — 07:00 daily. Change the hour/minute to match your wake time. Uses standard [cron syntax](https://crontab.guru/).\n/root/.openclaw/workspace/skills/briefing/README.md:87:- `--channel` — the channel where the briefing should be delivered (e.g. `telegram`, `discord`, `slack`).\n/root/.openclaw/workspace/skills/briefing/README.md:93:openclaw cron list\n/root/.openclaw/workspace/skills/briefing/README.md:98:- This uses OpenClaw's built-in cron scheduler — no external tools or system crontabs needed.\n/root/.openclaw/workspace/skills/briefing/README.md:99:- The cron job sends `/briefing` as a user message, which triggers the skill normally.\n/root/.openclaw/workspace/skills/briefing/README.md:101:- If the gateway restarts, cron jobs are reloaded automatically from `~/.openclaw/cron/jobs.json`.\n/root/.openclaw/workspace/skills/briefing/_meta.json:3:  \"slug\": \"briefing\",\n/root/.openclaw/workspace/skills/capability-evolver/src/gep/a2aProtocol.js:483:function _scheduleNextHeartbeat(delayMs) {\n/root/.openclaw/workspace/skills/capability-evolver/src/gep/a2aProtocol.