{"type":"message","id":"67b9886c","parentId":"7d0f3714","timestamp":"2026-03-22T02:31:29.136Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"**Investigating execution issues**\n\nI need to figure out why the run didn't execute. It seems like there’s neither a runs file nor any execution logs available. Maybe the isolated cron requires an agent ID? I see that the list shows an Agent ID, but maybe none was selected, which might explain why it got enqueued but didn’t actually run. I think it’s time to inspect the docs or help sections, especially regarding isolated cron runs and their defaults.","thinkingSignature":"{\"id\":\"rs_01bb7c6add707f1f0169bf5475141881918df287b3f42bba6e\",\"type\":\"reasoning\",\"encrypted_content\":\"gAAAAABpv1R58Pf8Jlv3DjmOUXr9xEA6xuLjogWdQ-xtAYiSFgw1lyMYxvDYSCXkIF2WLMArQjKRTeXa1gDJPUNx4YrhWyRsXqjGl5nCMRo2n7iRBJiheaiOSDJUsNgPng4bwd8Va4EW76nWrpxTMF6u57fAlCmjUVC6oVT5tE_ei31bc9BclYPVcHfBBf2dNAkInFdGYydYS6JANnRuVK1EHDGqS3CBqAvj28KZXX5J-U2_FVntcWzj4zz9sV1cNKsvoYpnEgQDPLLHs5nPU24-Iz8ayHbGKWdhINV7XSs41T5NmWMJzhs9JzsdxbmrtoIchtjl77QvQ5uzk4HZI1SyC7zNt4iGntzBWT9L2ApMMhZHGLWRS4bvsXW_WsNMWpahVCewN4fmSkA9CiBQ_L1IPnzHVpTs5cGAM9387j0eeNtJSEsUCbCN7Wo2kYhZ6W69Btlx0DwIWYOOwrSm23mgJ3Ul16jyEOziQ_cxYn4zGq0JqOGXOaCVKsH_Wub-dB-9FCY5PGk4jbtR2yN4lhdt8q0j0ipxPXsO3uuSurR0c8-llYYmOi4TL_nsWM6WKDzxBQMrQWNOC_kFRPcyT3VebgeoQ3iu-fdLKp8ZJ4QJOR77Xei2utzPFElqo6fVxYPEuSvQYPHPbAGgzpudO9iRGL5UzJGYl0uyLYWDKnIMYcro5TrJmuNK0Nmjc7IDeg2zMaPYMrlDAR0zQE4re-2d483ae-8RnC6lwnKZbHnJYVgkYlMJgIriuUjStKR5BmEU178Wckrn9OXIN3u7S65VsQR8N1fPbSxmoBkLHAbQ5o9H2SOTZvK-DK41-T6TsEavBWv13CGpixld-s5Ar-bEJijnCX1JrXOBHMb7cVa-QSEVCHeWD905ASNTKla7xfgubkm-vMO_rr1jymbvmZNbyz1_56FbUpNFDCnrtKsAgTEknI5KheyeV8Rb-2kZjIq0iq7Iy01g912YSaEmdIcLkrreoiBqNgT-GvmTVGFiyoHzuLNTKJq-tlMfR7WKGEJl-oatl9nqFlmYhR1E1XoK15wZKu_VizoWwcIWPVwZNTiAfFp72cnCekI44UZZm4pHkzO8QO3ZzmMAVZlO858S1v37WwTvViHuWLqDLtb0rbP6AuPxeiTrFzO1Uy3O34xwuX8W0yVQOeanzAJ4b0trdQpKXUpglhmBrlDkrmJ6Wp8xkpnee0vnpgn2QAlqh2hKH5ARa7FELatQqb4chz1zb5FqUYAYF5HRlsOqNByzZbaa9nWq40QFYbAs69Q-8KSUY_Z_4wqEkwvMvuVa9l2lnBWQlOSyrA==\",\"summary\":[{\"type\":\"summary_text\",\"text\":\"**Investigating execution issues**\\n\\nI need to figure out why the run didn't execute. It seems like there’s neither a runs file nor any execution logs available. Maybe the isolated cron requires an agent ID? I see that the list shows an Agent ID, but maybe none was selected, which might explain why it got enqueued but didn’t actually run. I think it’s time to inspect the docs or help sections, especially regarding isolated cron runs and their defaults.\"}]}"},{"type":"text","text":"我定位到一个新问题：**任务能入队，但没有真正开始执行。**  \n现在继续查“为什么没跑起来”，重点看 `cron run` 的实际语义和是否缺少隔离任务必需字段。","textSignature":"{\"v\":1,\"id\":\"msg_01bb7c6add707f1f0169bf547960e88191bc5539c290c23ebf\",\"phase\":\"commentary\"}"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_trEMTl48a5ddfDBKajkPxXtw|fc_01bb7c6add707f1f0169bf547ece9481918495e191db81c602","name":"exec","arguments":{"command":"openclaw cron runs --help","workdir":"/root/.openclaw/workspace","yieldMs":10000,"timeout":20},"partialJson":"{\"command\":\"openclaw cron runs --help\",\"workdir\":\"/root/.openclaw/workspace\",\"yieldMs\":10000,\"timeout\":20}"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_YFVBOiTtGm7KJXdVWuVSHIfm|fc_01bb7c6add707f1f0169bf547ecfd8819187f7404c0b17d63c","name":"exec","arguments":{"command":"grep -RIn \"sessionTarget.*isolated\\|agentId\\|delivery.mode\\|cron run\" /root/.local/share/pnpm/global/5/.pnpm/openclaw@2026.3.11_@napi-rs+canvas@0.1.97_@types+express@5.0.6_node-llama-cpp@3.16.2/node_modules/openclaw/docs/automation/cron-jobs.md /root/.local/share/pnpm/global/5/.pnpm/openclaw@2026.3.11_@napi-rs+canvas@0.1.97_@types+express@5.0.6_node-llama-cpp@3.16.2/node_modules/openclaw/docs/zh-CN/automation/cron-jobs.md | head -120","workdir":"/root/.openclaw/workspace","yieldMs":10000,"timeout":20},"partialJson":"{\"command\":\"grep -RIn \\\"sessionTarget.*isolated\\\\|agentId\\\\|delivery.mode\\\\|cron run\\\" /root/.local/share/pnpm/global/5/.pnpm/openclaw@2026.3.11_@napi-rs+canvas@0.1.97_@types+express@5.0.6_node-llama-cpp@3.16.2/node_modules/openclaw/docs/automation/cron-jobs.md /root/.local/share/pnpm/global/5/.pnpm/openclaw@2026.3.11_@napi-rs+canvas@0.1.97_@types+express@5.0.6_node-llama-cpp@3.16.2/node_modules/openclaw/docs/zh-CN/automation/cron-jobs.md | head -120\",\"workdir\":\"/root/.openclaw/workspace\",\"yieldMs\":10000,\"timeout\":20}"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_43WwC0P9rCnErOjCn5IMUz2d|fc_01bb7c6add707f1f0169bf547ecfe08191835fbbad7db0d26e","name":"exec","arguments":{"command":"grep -RIn \"manual:morning-briefing\\|agentTurn\\|delivery\\|announce\\|cron run\" /root/.local/share/pnpm/global/5/.pnpm/openclaw@2026.3.11_@napi-rs+canvas@0.1.97_@types+express@5.0.6_node-llama-cpp@3.16.2/node_modules/openclaw/dist | head -120","workdir":"/root/.openclaw/workspace","yieldMs":10000,"timeout":20},"partialJson":"{\"command\":\"grep -RIn \\\"manual:morning-briefing\\\\|agentTurn\\\\|delivery\\\\|announce\\\\|cron run\\\" /root/.local/share/pnpm/global/5/.pnpm/openclaw@2026.3.11_@napi-rs+canvas@0.1.97_@types+express@5.0.6_node-llama-cpp@3.16.2/node_modules/openclaw/dist | head -120\",\"workdir\":\"/root/.openclaw/workspace\",\"yieldMs\":10000,\"timeout\":20}"}],"api":"openai-codex-responses","provider":"openai-codex","model":"gpt-5.4","usage":{"input":8138,"output":538,"cacheRead":102656,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":111332,"cost":{"input":0.020345000000000002,"output":0.00807,"cacheRead":0.025664,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0.054079}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1774146673458}}
{"type":"message","id":"93caeff6","parentId":"67b9886c","timestamp":"2026-03-22T02:31:31.873Z","message":{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"call_trEMTl48a5ddfDBKajkPxXtw|fc_01bb7c6add707f1f0169bf547ece9481918495e191db81c602","toolName":"exec","content":[{"type":"text","text":"🦞 OpenClaw 2026.3.11 (29dc654) — We ship features faster than Apple ships calculator updates.\n\nUsage: openclaw cron runs [options]\n\nShow cron run history (JSONL-backed)\n\nOptions:\n  --expect-final   Wait for final response (agent) (default: false)\n  -h, --help       Display help for command\n  --id <id>        Job id\n  --limit <n>      Max entries (default 50) (default: \"50\")\n  --timeout <ms>   Timeout in ms (default: \"30000\")\n  --token <token>  Gateway token (if required)\n  --url <url>      Gateway WebSocket URL (defaults to gateway.remote.url when\n                   configured)"}],"details":{"status":"completed","exitCode":0,"durationMs":2725,"aggregated":"🦞 OpenClaw 2026.3.11 (29dc654) — We ship features faster than Apple ships calculator updates.\n\nUsage: openclaw cron runs [options]\n\nShow cron run history (JSONL-backed)\n\nOptions:\n  --expect-final   Wait for final response (agent) (default: false)\n  -h, --help       Display help for command\n  --id <id>        Job id\n  --limit <n>      Max entries (default 50) (default: \"50\")\n  --timeout <ms>   Timeout in ms (default: \"30000\")\n  --token <token>  Gateway token (if required)\n  --url <url>      Gateway WebSocket URL (defaults to gateway.remote.url when\n                   configured)","cwd":"/root/.openclaw/workspace"},"isError":false,"timestamp":1774146691861}}
{"type":"message","id":"509ffae4","parentId":"93caeff6","timestamp":"2026-03-22T02:31:31.892Z","message":{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"call_YFVBOiTtGm7KJXdVWuVSHIfm|fc_01bb7c6add707f1f0169bf547ecfd8819187f7404c0b17d63c","toolName":"exec","content":[{"type":"text","text":"/root/.local/share/pnpm/global/5/.pnpm/openclaw@2026.3.11_@napi-rs+canvas@0.1.97_@types+express@5.0.6_node-llama-cpp@3.16.2/node_modules/openclaw/docs/automation/cron-jobs.md:30:- Webhook posting is per job via `delivery.mode = \"webhook\"` + `delivery.to = \"<url>\"`.\n/root/.local/share/pnpm/global/5/.pnpm/openclaw@2026.3.11_@napi-rs+canvas@0.1.97_@types+express@5.0.6_node-llama-cpp@3.16.2/node_modules/openclaw/docs/automation/cron-jobs.md:31:- Legacy fallback remains for stored jobs with `notify: true` when `cron.webhook` is set, migrate those jobs to webhook delivery mode.\n/root/.local/share/pnpm/global/5/.pnpm/openclaw@2026.3.11_@napi-rs+canvas@0.1.97_@types+express@5.0.6_node-llama-cpp@3.16.2/node_modules/openclaw/docs/automation/cron-jobs.md:48:openclaw cron run <job-id>\n/root/.local/share/pnpm/global/5/.pnpm/openclaw@2026.3.11_@napi-rs+canvas@0.1.97_@types+express@5.0.6_node-llama-cpp@3.16.2/node_modules/openclaw/docs/automation/cron-jobs.md:49:openclaw cron runs --id <job-id>\n/root/.local/share/pnpm/global/5/.pnpm/openclaw@2026.3.11_@napi-rs+canvas@0.1.97_@types+express@5.0.6_node-llama-cpp@3.16.2/node_modules/openclaw/docs/automation/cron-jobs.md:88:   - `sessionTarget: \"isolated\"` → run a dedicated agent turn in `cron:<jobId>`.\n/root/.local/share/pnpm/global/5/.pnpm/openclaw@2026.3.11_@napi-rs+canvas@0.1.97_@types+express@5.0.6_node-llama-cpp@3.16.2/node_modules/openclaw/docs/automation/cron-jobs.md:105:- optional **delivery mode** (`announce`, `webhook`, or `none`).\n/root/.local/share/pnpm/global/5/.pnpm/openclaw@2026.3.11_@napi-rs+canvas@0.1.97_@types+express@5.0.6_node-llama-cpp@3.16.2/node_modules/openclaw/docs/automation/cron-jobs.md:106:- optional **agent binding** (`agentId`): run the job under a specific agent; if\n/root/.local/share/pnpm/global/5/.pnpm/openclaw@2026.3.11_@napi-rs+canvas@0.1.97_@types+express@5.0.6_node-llama-cpp@3.16.2/node_modules/openclaw/docs/automation/cron-jobs.md:156:- Default behavior: if `delivery` is omitted, isolated jobs announce a summary (`delivery.mode = \"announce\"`).\n/root/.local/share/pnpm/global/5/.pnpm/openclaw@2026.3.11_@napi-rs+canvas@0.1.97_@types+express@5.0.6_node-llama-cpp@3.16.2/node_modules/openclaw/docs/automation/cron-jobs.md:157:- `delivery.mode` chooses what happens:\n/root/.local/share/pnpm/global/5/.pnpm/openclaw@2026.3.11_@napi-rs+canvas@0.1.97_@types+express@5.0.6_node-llama-cpp@3.16.2/node_modules/openclaw/docs/automation/cron-jobs.md:184:- `delivery.mode`: `none` | `announce` | `webhook`.\n/root/.local/share/pnpm/global/5/.pnpm/openclaw@2026.3.11_@napi-rs+canvas@0.1.97_@types+express@5.0.6_node-llama-cpp@3.16.2/node_modules/openclaw/docs/automation/cron-jobs.md:190:to target the chat instead. When `delivery.mode = \"none\"`, no summary is posted to the main session.\n/root/.local/share/pnpm/global/5/.pnpm/openclaw@2026.3.11_@napi-rs+canvas@0.1.97_@types+express@5.0.6_node-llama-cpp@3.16.2/node_modules/openclaw/docs/automation/cron-jobs.md:196:When `delivery.mode = \"announce\"`, cron delivers directly via the outbound channel adapters.\n/root/.local/share/pnpm/global/5/.pnpm/openclaw@2026.3.11_@napi-rs+canvas@0.1.97_@types+express@5.0.6_node-llama-cpp@3.16.2/node_modules/openclaw/docs/automation/cron-jobs.md:207:- A short summary is posted to the main session only when `delivery.mode = \"announce\"`.\n/root/.local/share/pnpm/global/5/.pnpm/openclaw@2026.3.11_@napi-rs+canvas@0.1.97_@types+express@5.0.6_node-llama-cpp@3.16.2/node_modules/openclaw/docs/automation/cron-jobs.md:213:When `delivery.mode = \"webhook\"`, cron posts the finished event payload to `delivery.to` when the finished event includes a summary.\n/root/.local/share/pnpm/global/5/.pnpm/openclaw@2026.3.11_@napi-rs+canvas@0.1.97_@types+express@5.0.6_node-llama-cpp@3.16.2/node_modules/openclaw/docs/automation/cron-jobs.md:221:- Deprecated fallback: stored legacy jobs with `notify: true` still post to `cron.webhook` (if configured), with a warning so you can migrate to `delivery.mode = \"webhook\"`.\n/root/.local/share/pnpm/global/5/.pnpm/openclaw@2026.3.11_@napi-rs+canvas@0.1.97_@types+express@5.0.6_node-llama-cpp@3.16.2/node_modules/openclaw/docs/automation/cron-jobs.md:252:- `delivery.mode`: `announce` (channel delivery), `webhook` (HTTP POST), or `none`.\n/root/.local/share/pnpm/global/5/.pnpm/openclaw@2026.3.11_@napi-rs+canvas@0.1.97_@types+express@5.0.6_node-llama-cpp@3.16.2/node_modules/openclaw/docs/automation/cron-jobs.md:256:`announce` delivery is only valid for isolated jobs (`sessionTarget: \"isolated\"`).\n/root/.local/share/pnpm/global/5/.pnpm/openclaw@2026.3.11_@napi-rs+canvas@0.1.97_@types+express@5.0.6_node-llama-cpp@3.16.2/node_modules/openclaw/docs/automation/cron-jobs.md:308:  \"sessionTarget\": \"isolated\",\n/root/.local/share/pnpm/global/5/.pnpm/openclaw@2026.3.11_@napi-rs+canvas@0.1.97_@types+express@5.0.6_node-llama-cpp@3.16.2/node_modules/openclaw/docs/automation/cron-jobs.md:329:- `sessionTarget` must be `\"main\"` or `\"isolated\"` and must match `payload.kind`.\n/root/.local/share/pnpm/global/5/.pnpm/openclaw@2026.3.11_@napi-rs+canvas@0.1.97_@types+express@5.0.6_node-llama-cpp@3.16.2/node_modules/openclaw/docs/automation/cron-jobs.md:330:- Optional fields: `agentId`, `description`, `enabled`, `deleteAfterRun` (defaults to true for `at`),\n/root/.local/share/pnpm/global/5/.pnpm/openclaw@2026.3.11_@napi-rs+canvas@0.1.97_@types+express@5.0.6_node-llama-cpp@3.16.2/node_modules/openclaw/docs/automation/cron-jobs.md:349:- Use `agentId: null` in the patch to clear an agent binding.\n/root/.local/share/pnpm/global/5/.pnpm/openclaw@2026.3.11_@napi-rs+canvas@0.1.97_@types+express@5.0.6_node-llama-cpp@3.16.2/node_modules/openclaw/docs/automation/cron-jobs.md:365:- Isolated cron run sessions in `sessions.json` are pruned by `cron.sessionRetention` (default `24h`; set `false` to disable).\n/root/.local/share/pnpm/global/5/.pnpm/openclaw@2026.3.11_@napi-rs+canvas@0.1.97_@types+express@5.0.6_node-llama-cpp@3.16.2/node_modules/openclaw/docs/automation/cron-jobs.md:434:- Preferred: set `delivery.mode: \"webhook\"` with `delivery.to: \"https://...\"` per job.\n/root/.local/share/pnpm/global/5/.pnpm/openclaw@2026.3.11_@napi-rs+canvas@0.1.97_@types+express@5.0.6_node-llama-cpp@3.16.2/node_modules/openclaw/docs/automation/cron-jobs.md:479:- review growth periodically with `openclaw cron runs` and adjust retention before logs become large\n/root/.local/share/pnpm/global/5/.pnpm/openclaw@2026.3.11_@napi-rs+canvas@0.1.97_@types+express@5.0.6_node-llama-cpp@3.16.2/node_modules/openclaw/docs/automation/cron-jobs.md:621:openclaw cron run <jobId>\n/root/.local/share/pnpm/global/5/.pnpm/openclaw@2026.3.11_@napi-rs+canvas@0.1.97_@types+express@5.0.6_node-llama-cpp@3.16.2/node_modules/openclaw/docs/automation/cron-jobs.md:622:openclaw cron run <jobId> --due\n/root/.local/share/pnpm/global/5/.pnpm/openclaw@2026.3.11_@napi-rs+canvas@0.1.97_@types+express@5.0.6_node-llama-cpp@3.16.2/node_modules/openclaw/docs/automation/cron-jobs.md:625:`cron.run` now acknowledges once the manual run is queued, not after the job finishes. Successful queue responses look like `{ ok: true, enqueued: true, runId }`. If the job is already running or `--due` finds nothing due, the response stays `{ ok: true, ran: false, reason }`. Use `openclaw cron runs --id <jobId>` or the `cron.runs` gateway method to inspect the eventual finished entry.\n/root/.local/share/pnpm/global/5/.pnpm/openclaw@2026.3.11_@napi-rs+canvas@0.1.97_@types+express@5.0.6_node-llama-cpp@3.16.2/node_modules/openclaw/docs/automation/cron-jobs.md:645:openclaw cron runs --id <jobId> --limit 50\n/root/.local/share/pnpm/global/5/.pnpm/openclaw@2026.3.11_@napi-rs+canvas@0.1.97_@types+express@5.0.6_no